 "note": [
  "Take Root API is egress-blocked from this container (curl to api.takeroot.bible returns 000). The IRV was fetched instead from the ebible mirror on raw.githubusercontent.com (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx — that collection serves USX, not USFM), all 66 books / 31,104 verses, and every span marked mined was lifted from it with a script rather than typed.",
  "Derived by measurement, not from a translator's report: each quoted span was byte-matched against the IRV verse it cites, blind only to our own quotation marks. 47 of 55 distinct references matched; the rest are the review queue.",
  "Quotation marks MIRROR the English source, which is what the six shipped Hindi books do — 6 of 6 pairs reproduce their source's marks exactly, including clothed-with-strength-and-dignity carrying its source's 104 &quot; entities. Citations follow the shipped corpus: Western digits (3,252 against 0 Devanagari) and a tight C:V colon (364 of 367).",
  "This book carries 11 BODY_CORRECTIONS entries plus a source_fixes repair on ch09, so the chapters were prepped through apply_body_corrections + apply_source_fixes and the CORRECTED text was translated — the fixture keeps the defects and the release chain repairs the rows on deploy, so prepping straight from the fixture would have handed known defects into a new language.",
  "ENGLISH, found not fixed: ch08 opens «1 Timothy 1:15 umility is often identified...» — the chapter's first letter is missing, a dropped drop-cap. Rendered as the intended word, the same call BODY_CORRECTIONS already makes for L ORD. Also, &#x27; appears undecoded throughout this fixture (as it does in he-holds-my-tomorrows), which is why the per-block digit check reports phantom 27s.",
  "ch02 opens with a paragraph whose quotation marks are garbled in the English (no opening mark, and a stray “ before the citation). Rendered as plain scripture with the citation at the end — which is exactly what the shipped Spanish, Arabic and Portuguese editions of this book all do at the same paragraph.",
  "The 8 unverified references fall into two kinds, both conservative rather than composed. (a) The author ABRIDGES a verse mid-sentence to fit his argument — John 5:30 stops at «I seek not my own will», John 6:38 at «not to do my own», John 8:28 at «I can do nothing on my own» — so the Hindi carries the IRV's words but not a contiguous stretch of them. (b) The citation joins NON-ADJACENT verses (Matthew 5:3,5 skips 5:4; 1 Corinthians 15:9,10; Matthew 20:27 where the quotation runs on into 20:28), so the joined span cannot match the IRV contiguously even though each verse does. Both are listed unverified deliberately: it is better to overstate the review queue than to let an abridged quotation read as checked."
 ]
